{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"GATES (exit codes, from the worktree venv, branch fix/f81d-e3cd-caching @ 25f5146dc0):\n\n  make lint       -> 0\n  make typecheck  -> 0  (mypy, 416 source files, no issues)\n  make test       -> 2  (9130 passed, 41 skipped, 178 deselected, 1 FAILED in 29m47s)\n\nThe single failure is NOT from this change and is PROVEN pre-existing:\n\n  tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py::test_success_telemetry_survives_an_empty_usage_dict\n  StopIteration\n\nIt passes in isolation (12 passed) and is order-dependent. Root cause reproduced on a CLEAN\ncheckout with this change STASHED: `review_bot/config.py:145-146 configure_logging()` sets\n`logging.getLogger(\"rebar\").propagate = False` process-globally and never restores it, after which\npytest's caplog (a ROOT-logger handler) can never see a `rebar.*` record again. Filed as\nb718-fb7f-b1a4-4feb (available-batty-kagu), linked discovered_from this ticket, with the two-test\nreproduction. Nothing in this change touches logging, agent_call, or review_bot, and\n`estimate_marked_prefix_tokens` is unreachable on the unit-test path (it requires\n`model_override is None`).\n\nBase note: the suite ran at 9ca172baa2. origin/main has since advanced 3 commits, all touching only\ntests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py, which the default selection deselects (`-m \"not\nintegration and not external\"`) - so the drift cannot affect this result.\n\nREPLICATION of the original report through the real predicate (constructed call, no paid run):\n\n  coach_notes           sonnet-4-6  floor 1024  marked 150  total 7078\n    -> \"CANNOT engage: only 150 tokens sit ahead of the cache breakpoint, below this model's\n        1024-token minimum, while 6928 of the 7078 billed input tokens ride AFTER it unmarked\"\n  enrich/ticket-digest  haiku-4-5   floor 4096  marked 477  total 6803\n    -> \"CANNOT engage: only 477 tokens sit ahead of the cache breakpoint, below this model's\n        4096-token minimum, while 6326 of the 6803 billed input tokens ride AFTER it unmarked\"\n\nBoth now name the marked prefix and the model's floor. Under the old predicate the first reported\n`input_tokens=7078` against a blind 4096 and the second was silent on haiku.\n\nCommit: 25f5146dc053e929de3c565e14caed9116a68b6c (not pushed to Gerrit, per instruction)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785724449749384001,"uuid":"ecc49c24-1549-41e9-be71-535ab1efd900"}